<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tarqui</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1829</span> · Also known as Battle of Portete de Tarqui · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gran-colombia-peru-war">Gran Colombia–Peru War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Tarqui was fought on 27 February 1829 at Portete de Tarqui near Cuenca in modern Ecuador. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombian forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-jose-de-sucre">Antonio José de Sucre</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-jose-flores">Juan José Flores</a> defeated the Peruvian army of President José de La Mar. The victory saved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guayaquil">Guayaquil</a> for Gran Colombia and led to a peace treaty later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tarqui.jpg" alt="Battle of Tarqui" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jefferson · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batalla-de-tarqui.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
